>
>>
> The program I used to generate the clusters counted "j" as a sibilant, but
> not as voiced. If I add "j" to the voiced consonants, 10 unused clusters go
> away, leaving 19 unused out of 179 total medial clusters:
>
>    - bg
>    - bz
>    - dl
>    - dm
>    - fm
>    - fp
>    - fx
>    - gm
>    - gz
>    - jg
>    - lz
>    - mv
>    - pf
>    - px
>    - sf
>    - xm
>    - xp
>    - xt
>    - zv
>
>
Interesting, thanks. Three of them (jg, sf and zv) are valid initials, so
that means these three are the only ones that occur as initial CC (jgari,
sfasa, zvati) but not as medial CC.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

